- IDEA: for all of the "write down steps to" things listed in this
  document (wdst), I'm wondering if I could make them "modular", in the
  sense that you could specify which ones you want (as arguments to
  `build-image.sh`, I think), and then the `setup.sh` in your image will
  create a `/bin/initial-setup` that includes all the "modules" you
  want.  So on top of the base setup, you can choose the

  - http module, caddy variant
  - interactive qol module
  - doas module (nb, setting the alp user's password will *always*
    require the human)
  - man pages module (Q: is there a way to tell apk to always install
    the associated "-doc" package when the package itself is installed?)
  - cron module (not sure this is necessary or useful)
  - remote desktop module (although I've tried now to get this going
    with wayland *and* with xrdp/remmina, and neither worked out)

  I'm not sure how complex this would be, and maybe it isn't worth it
  (and just taking an ad hoc approach to "enabling" these "modules" is
  totally fine).

